From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:15:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): restart hands running turns over at a step
 boundary

gateway.restart_turn_handoff_boundary (false = off), with restart_turn_handoff: a graceful restart no longer stops each running turn mid-step (cutting a streamed reply or a foreground command) and continues it with a synthetic "Hermes restarted" message. It asks each turn to stop at its next step boundary, waiting up to restart_turn_handoff_wait_seconds: after a model call that is fully streamed and stored, or after a tool round whose results are stored. The turn ends with no reply, failed-turn row or notice, and its admission goes back to its FIFO place with a resume record (state_meta gateway.turn_resume.v1.<admission>).

A turn parked on its own clarify question or approval card counts as at a boundary. The record keeps each prompt (id, card, smart verdict); the call that raised it stays unexecuted and unwritten. The prompt stays answerable on the old gateway until it exits (the answer goes into the record), and the next gateway registers it under the same id before any claim.

The next gateway claims the admission like any queued one; the claim takes the record in the same write. message.start carries resumed: true and no text. The turn reuses its stored rows (no second user row), runs only the tool calls its last step left without a result, then calls the model. A re-raised clarify or approval adopts the handed-over prompt: same id, no new card, no second smart review, an answer already given is read at once.

A turn still between boundaries when the wait ends, or one run by a managed worker, is stopped and continued as restart_turn_handoff does.
